<===> README.md
This mixin should load modules in the same way as the `@use` rule. To avoid tons
of duplicated tests, we just test a couple basic error cases.

<===>
================================================================================
<===> missing/input.scss
@use "sass:meta";
$_: meta.load("other");

<===> missing/error
Error: Can't find stylesheet to import.
  ,
2 | $_: meta.load("other");
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:5  root stylesheet

<===>
================================================================================
<===> loop/input.scss
@use "sass:meta";
$_: meta.load("other");

<===> loop/_other.scss
@use "sass:meta";
c {d: meta.load("input")}

<===> loop/error
Error: Module loop: input.scss is already being loaded.
  ,
2 | c {d: meta.load("input")}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  _other.scss 2:7  load()
  input.scss 2:5   root stylesheet
